UPDATE companies SET description='Assembled Products, Inc. was founded in 1986 by Michael Stevens in Collierville, Tennessee, before relocating to Piperton, Tennessee in 1990 and later to a 33,000‑square‑foot facility in the Elgin community near Rogersville, Alabama. The company is woman‑owned and operates as a small business with approximately ten employees.

The shop provides printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) using surface‑mount, through‑hole, and mixed‑technology processes, along with electromechanical box builds, wire‑harness fabrication, conformal coating, and functional testing. In‑house capabilities extend to design‑for‑manufacturability review, repair and rework, 3D printing, CAD drawing, patent research, and new‑product consulting. The facility also houses machining, plastic molding, and urethane/resin casting equipment to support complete product development from prototype through low‑to‑medium‑volume production.

Named accounts have included Federal Express, AutoZone, the University of Memphis, Hypertech, and IBS, alongside individual inventors and hobbyists. The company serves the southeastern United States — Alabama, Tennessee, Mississippi, Georgia, and Florida — as well as national clients.

