UPDATE companies SET description='Atlas Precision Inc. traces its roots to April 1979, when Johann W. Hofschuster founded Atlas Mold Inc. in Arden, North Carolina, to design and build injection molds. In 1988 the company added a custom molding division, Atlas Precision Plastics, and installed its first molding machines the following year. The two operations were combined under one roof in 2006, and the business has remained under Hofschuster''s leadership as president and chief executive.

Today the firm operates as a full-service injection molder with 33 presses ranging from 80 to 360 tons, each equipped with a robot or sprue picker. The production floor runs 24/7 across four crews, supported by an on-site toolroom that designs, builds, and maintains multi-cavity tooling, including core-pull, unscrewing, overmolding, and hot-runner systems. A quality lab and RJG/eDart process monitoring complement the molding operation, while 3D printing provides prototype parts. The company works with engineered resins and wood-composite materials.

Atlas serves the healthcare, automotive, telecommunications, industrial, and electrical markets, producing components for medical devices, electrical connectors, packaging, and single-use consumer products. Long-standing customers include Johnson & Johnson (Personal Care and Vistakon divisions), S.C. Johnson, Bic Corporation, Robert Bosch Automotive, Tyco Electronics, and Trex.

The company emphasizes a one-stop-shop model, assigning each customer a dedicated account manager who coordinates design, tooling, molding, and packaging. Hofschuster''s team highlights its reputation for building fast-cycling, low-maintenance tooling and holds ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, CSA International, and UL certifications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','CSA International','UL (Underwriters Laboratories)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Tool design and construction", "Mold flow analysis", "Prototyping via 3D printing", "Overmolding", "Core-pull and unscrewing mold actuation", "Hot-runner systems", "High-volume, tight-tolerance molding", "Multi-cavity tooling", "Material selection and polymer expertise", "Packaging", "RJG/eDart process control", "Quality inspection and lab testing"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Automotive", "Telecommunications", "Industrial", "Electrical", "Medical devices", "Packaging", "Consumer products"], "materials": ["Engineered plastics", "Wood composite"], "equipment": ["33 injection molding machines (80\u2013360 ton)", "Robots/sprue pickers on each press", "RJG/eDart process monitoring systems", "3D printer for prototype parts", "On-site toolroom for mold design and build"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dedicated account manager for each customer", "On-site tool design, building, and maintenance", "24/7 production across four crews", "33 molding machines (80\u2013360 ton) with robotic part handling", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certified for medical and general quality"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 by Johann W. Hofschuster in Arden, NC -> /about-us", "Atlas Mold established April 1979; Atlas Precision Plastics added 1988; combined 2006 -> /about-us", "33 molding machines 80-360 ton, each with robot/sprue picker -> /about-us", "24/7 production with four crews -> /about-us", "On-site tool building capability, design and build own t