UPDATE companies SET description='Headquartered in Ogden, Utah, Autoliv North America operates as the U.S. arm of the global Autoliv group, the world''s largest automotive safety supplier.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures passive safety systems — including airbags, seatbelts, steering wheels, and pyrotechnical safety switches — for virtually every major automaker. It also produces mobility safety solutions such as a motorcycle airbag vest developed with RS Taichi. Autoliv runs 13 technical centers and 20 test tracks across 25 countries, employing roughly 65,000 people, and reported $10.8 billion in net sales for 2025.

Its customers span the automotive industry, commercial vehicle manufacturers, and emerging mobility sectors. Recent collaborations include partnerships with XPENG and Great Wall Motor to advance safer mobility worldwide, and the RS Taichi venture brings motorcycle safety gear to market.

Autoliv states its mission is "Saving More Lives," citing that its products saved an estimated 40,000 lives and prevented 600,000 injuries in 2025. The company has set a target of carbon-neutral operations by 2030 and emphasizes digitalization and automation as cornerstones of its operational excellence.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Passive safety system design and development", "Airbag manufacturing", "Seatbelt manufacturing", "Steering wheel manufacturing", "Pyrotechnical safety switch production", "Motorcycle airbag vest development", "Test services (including virtual testing)", "Digitalization and automation integration"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Motorcycle safety gear", "Commercial vehicle safety", "Mobility safety solutions"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["13 technical centers and 20 test tracks globally", "Products saved 40,000 lives in 2025", "Targeting carbon-neutral operations by 2030", "Digitalization and automation as operational cornerstones"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Ogden, Utah -> db", "World''s largest automotive safety supplier -> /", "~65,000 colleagues worldwide -> /", "Operations in 25 countries, 13 technical centers, 20 test tracks -> /, /about-us", "Designs, develops, manufactures passive safety systems: airbags, seatbelts, steering wheels -> /about-us", "Pyrotechnical safety switches -> /", "Motorcycle airbag vest developed with RS Taichi -> db", "Net sales $10.8 billion in 2025 -> /about-us", "Products saved 40,000 lives and reduced 600,000 injuries in 2025 -> /about-us", "Partnerships with XPENG and Great Wall Motor -> /", "Carbon-neutral operations target by 2030 -> /", "Digitalization and automation as operational cornerstones -> /about-us", "Test services offered -> db", "Global presence in 25 countries -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Through our group companies, we develop, manufacture and market protective systems, such as airbags, seatbelts, and steering wheels for all major automotive manufacturers in the world as well as mobility safety solutions.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "~65,000", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='autoliv-north-america-inc-otc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Automated Food Systems, based in Waxahachie, Texas, was founded in 1976 by mechanical engineer Glenn Walser. With a single investor, Walser developed the world''s first automated corn dog system after a food processor sought a method to automate production—a challenge others deemed impossible.

The company designs, manufactures, and integrates custom food processing and material handling equipment for stick and skewered foods. Its product line includes corn dog systems (3,000–16,000 units per hour), kebab and skewer systems (up to 4,080 units per hour), funnel cake systems, market-entry systems, industrial batter mixers (60–180 gallon capacities), food pumps (up to 223 GPM), and food-grade skewers and sticks. Equipment is built to withstand harsh processing environments and is customized to each facility''s space and process requirements.

Customers range from small producers to the largest multinational food processing companies, with installations across North America, South America, Africa, Europe, Asia, and Australia. The company serves the corn dog, kebab, funnel cake, and broader industrial food manufacturing sectors.

AFS emphasizes service and support for the life of each system, including a dedicated parts inventory, on-site training, plant layout optimization, and custom design and fabrication for unique food automation challenges. The business began with a single problem-solving mission and continues to engineer solutions for unique food processing challenges.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom design & fabrication", "Maintenance assistance", "Training & consultation", "Plant layout optimization", "Automated corn dog production", "Kebab and skewer assembly", "Funnel cake frying", "Batter mixing", "Food pumping", "Skewer and stick insertion", "Material handling", "System integration"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Corn dog production", "Kebab and skewer production", "Funnel cake production", "Concessions", "Industrial food manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["KW-2001 high-speed skewering system", "PTL-2600 fully automated corn dog system", "PTL-2100 fully automated corn dog system", "PTL-2000 fully automated corn dog system", "PTL-1200 semi-automated corn dog system", "PTL-1000 semi-automated corn dog system", "HOP-1300 semi-automated corn dog system", "HOP-100 manual corn dog system", "MM-750 fifteen sack batter mixer", "MM-500 ten sack batter mixer", "MM-240 five-sack batter mixer", "MM Jr. one sack mixer", "HM-5 table top market-entry mixer", "CD-3 table top corn dog system", "CD-3 vendor cart", "SS-100 sausage sticking system", "Model 123 sanitary food transfer pump", "Model 200 sanitary food pump", "FC-950 funnel cake fryer and batter dispensing system", "PRL-400 semi-automated corn dog processing system"], "volume": "Corn dog systems: 3,000\u201316,000 units/hr; Kebab systems: up to 4,080 units/hr", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Service & support for the life of your system", "Custom design & fabrication for unique processes", "Equipment built to last decades under heavy use", "On-site training and consultation included with every installation", "Global installations across six continents"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1976 by Glenn Walser -> /about", "Headquarters Waxahachie, Texas -> db", "First automated corn dog system developed -> /about", "Product lines: corn dog systems (3,000-16,000 units/hr) -> /", "Kebab & skewer systems up to 4,080 units/hr -> /", "Funnel cake systems -> /", "Market entry systems -> /", "Mixers 60-180 gal -> /", "Food pumps up to 223 GPM -> /", "Commodities: food-grade skewers and sticks -> /", "Global installations across six continents -> /about", "Service & support for life of system -> /services", "Custom design & fabrication -> /services", "On-site training and consultation -> /services", "Plant layout optimization -> /services", "Equipment built to last decades -> /", "History of product models -> /about", "Company type: manufacturer -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in designing, manufacturing, and integrating the finest custom food processing equipment and material handling equipment for stick and skewered food industries", "founded_year": "1976", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='automated-food-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Automotive Charging & Starting LLC was founded in 2011 by Brian Webb in Idaho Falls, Idaho. Webb brought over 20 years of experience from AC&S to the venture, which operates as an independently owned and operated shop serving the local community and surrounding region.

The company provides battery sales, service, and recycling, along with repair services for alternators, starters, generators, and DC motors. It maintains a large inventory of parts from OEM and aftermarket suppliers such as Delco, Bosch, Denso, and Mitsubishi, and offers same-day completion on most jobs unless parts must be ordered. A 24-hour emergency service, free battery checks, free installation, and a battery buy-back program round out the service lineup.

Customers span automotive, commercial, industrial, agricultural, marine, and recreational sectors. The shop services all major vehicle manufacturers, including brands from Japan (Acura, Toyota, Honda), Europe (Audi, BMW, Mercedes-Benz), and the United States (Ford, Chevrolet, Ram, Jeep), as well as heavy-duty trucks, agricultural equipment, and marine deep-cycle applications.

