UPDATE companies SET description='Avon Lake Sheet Metal Company, Inc. has been family-owned and operated since 1953 in Avon Lake, Ohio, about 25 miles west of Cleveland. The business began in a one-car garage when founders George Wightman and Carl Wetzig Sr. established the shop on principles of honesty and hard work. Second-generation owners Carl Wetzig Jr. and Gary Wightman continue to lead the company today.

The company runs a 32,000-square-foot facility on a five-acre industrial site equipped with modern machinery including a Trumpf TruLaser 2030 4,000-watt fiber laser, a Trumpf TruBend 2100 press brake, a Wysong 12-foot 175-ton hydraulic press brake, a Lockformer Vulcan 2900 dual-table CNC plasma cutter, and a Fasti FP60 CNC panel former. Core capabilities span sheet metal fabrication (CNC laser, plasma, and shear cutting; CNC press brake forming and panel folding; rolling), structural fabrication (sawing, punching, drilling), certified welding (MIG, TIG, stick, flux core, pulsed MIG, spot, field), assembly of mechanical components and modules, finishing (painting, laser etching, glass beading, grinding), and 3D modeling with Inventor and AutoCAD. Field services cover equipment installation, field welding, plant maintenance, project management, and coordination drawings. The shop also provides turnkey HVAC system design, duct fabrication, and installation, plus custom machine guarding fabrication and installation.

Avon Lake Sheet Metal serves a diverse customer base across automotive, steel and foundry, chemical, plastics, construction, food processing, general manufacturing, retail, education, and health care industries. The company also works with medical groups, industrial mills, and bulk powder material handling systems.

The founders'' original emphasis on honesty, hard work, and lasting value remains central. The company states its core values as quality, efficiency, and integrity, and highlights a safety-first culture recognized by multiple SMACNA Zero Injury Awards (2015, 2017, 2018, 2020, 2022). AWS-certified welders and a drug-free workplace certification further underscore its operational standards.', certifications=ARRAY['SMACNA Zero Injury Award (2015, 2017, 2018, 2020, 2022)','AWS Certified Welders','Ohio License #18015','Ohio BWC Drug-Free Workplace']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC laser cutting", "CNC plasma cutting", "CNC shearing", "CNC press brake forming", "CNC panel folding", "Sheet and plate rolling", "Structural sawing", "Structural punching", "Structural drilling", "Pulsed MIG welding", "MIG welding", "Flux core welding", "Stick welding", "TIG welding", "Spot welding", "Field welding", "Assembly of mechanical components", "Assembly of modules or skids", "Special packaging and crating", "Laser etching", "Painting", "Glass beading", "Grinding and polishing", "3D modeling (Inventor)", "AutoCAD 2D drawing", "Design and fabrication drawings", "Coordination drawings", "Equipment installation", "Field welding", "Plant maintenance", "Project management", "Custom machine guarding fabrication and installation", "Turnkey HVAC system design and installation", "Duct fabrication and installation", "HVAC system service", "Dust collection system installation", "Pneumatic conveying system installation", "Bulk powder material handling system installation"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Steel and Foundry", "Chemical", "Plastics", "Construction", "Food Processing", "General Manufacturing", "Retail", "Education", "Health Care", "Medical", "Industrial Mills"], "materials": ["Sheet metal", "Structural steel"], "equipment": ["FMS Mitering Bandsaw", "Hougen \u2013 Nitto Magnetic Drills", "Wysong 1/4\" x 10 Hydraulic Shear CNC Front and Rear Gauging", "Wysong 12'' x 175 Ton Hydr