UPDATE companies SET description='Axles Plus, operating as the axle-assembly division of Custom Tool & Die, Inc., is based in Beebe, Arkansas. The parent company began in a small garage in 1979 and incorporated in April 1980, growing from a tool-and-die shop into a full-scale metal fabrication and manufacturing plant on Highway 5 near Cabot since 1982. The business remains third-generation family-owned and operated. In May 2015 the Axles Plus brand was launched in Ward, AR, and in 2017 the operation moved to its current Beebe location where axle assemblies are built and a retail store serves walk-in customers.

The company produces trailer axles, components, and accessories—including hardware kits, spring latch assemblies, and a range of nuts, bolts, and shackle straps. Production centers on CNC machining, laser cutting, metal fabrication, stamping, and custom manufacturing, allowing the shop to handle both small specialty projects and larger production runs. The facility also prepares trucks for in-state and out-of-state delivery.

Axles Plus serves the trailer industry, supplying equipment trailers, travel trailers, horse trailers, and other trailer types. Customers include individual trailer owners who visit the retail showroom for parts such as tongue hitches, trailer jacks, bearings, LED lights, and bulk tires and wheels, as well as commercial trailer builders needing custom axle assemblies.

The company emphasizes that customer service is its top goal and that quality is never optional, combining modern technology with American-made craftsmanship to deliver dependable products. It highlights its ability to adapt and invest in advanced production capabilities while maintaining the values that shaped the business.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining", "Laser cutting", "Metal fabrication", "Stamping", "Custom manufacturing", "Axle assembly", "Retail sales"], "industries": ["Trailer manufacturing", "Equipment trailers", "Travel trailers", "Horse trailers", "Trailer parts and accessories"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC machines", "Laser cutters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Third-generation family ownership", "In-house CNC machining, laser cutting, metal fabrication, and stamping", "Retail showroom for direct customer purchases", "In-state and out-of-state delivery fleet", "American-made trailer axles and components"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 as Custom Tool & Die, Inc. -> /", "Incorporated April 1980 -> /", "Located on Highway 5 near Cabot, Arkansas since 1982 -> /", "Axles Plus established May 2015 in Ward, AR -> /", "Moved to Beebe, Arkansas in 2017 for axle assembly and retail -> /", "Third-generation family-owned and operated -> /", "Processes: CNC machining, laser cutting, metal fabrication, stamping, custom manufacturing -> /", "Products: trailer axles, components, accessories, hardware kits, spring latch assemblies -> /", "Industries: equipment trailers, travel trailers, horse trailers -> /", "Retail showroom for parts: tongue hitches, trailer jacks, bearings, LED lights, bulk tires and wheels -> /", "Customer service is #1 goal, quality never optional -> /", "American-made craftsmanship -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Tool & Die, Inc. dba Axles Plus is a third generation, family owned and operated manufacturing company located in central Arkansas.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='axles-plus' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Axon Medical Technologies is based in New Cumberland, Pennsylvania. The company was founded in 2003 by Michael Zarreii, who serves as chief executive and chief scientific officer. Zarreii began the venture as a philanthropic effort to explore the connection between the brain’s involuntary sensory functions and cognition, aiming to develop advanced diagnostic and therapeutic devices.

The company designs and manufactures two primary platforms: ECAT™, a point-of-care multi-screening system for primary care clinics, and Intellig-EYES™, a neurological performance measurement headgear. Both are produced in an FDA-registered facility in the United States. The platforms automate assessments such as pupillometry, cognitive testing (Trail Making Test, GPCOG, MMSE, CAPS-5), and rapid concussion screening. Axon Medical is currently expanding its manufacturing capacity to serve both commercial and military markets.

The technology targets primary care and family practice clinics, as well as military healthcare settings. The U.S. Army has funded a four-year study to integrate ECAT and Intellig-EYES into treatment protocols for service members. The platforms also support sports medicine through sideline concussion detection. Customers include clinic owners and healthcare providers who lease the devices under a per-scan billing model with CPT code reimbursement.

Zarreii’s original vision was to solve complex neurological challenges through non-invasive, objective, and automated testing. The company differentiates itself with portable, lightweight devices that generate real-time, color-coded results and clinical documentation, all while minimizing financial risk for providers through a leasing structure rather than direct sales.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA-registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Point-of-care multi-screening (ECAT\u2122)", "Neurological performance measurement (Intellig-EYES\u2122)", "Automated pupillometry", "Cognitive assessment (Trail Making Test A/B, GPCOG, MMSE, CAPS-5)", "Concussion screening (Sideline Test, Cognitive Alertness Test)", "EMR integration (Epic, Cerner)", "Clinical documentation generation", "Device leasing and per-scan billing"], "industries": ["Primary care clinics", "Family practice clinics", "Military healthcare (U.S. Army)", "Sports medicine", "Neurology and psychiatry"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["ECAT\u2122 platform", "Intellig-EYES\u2122 headgear", "Pupillometry measurement system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Designed and manufactured in the USA in an FDA-registered facility", "Non-invasive, automated neurological and cognitive assessments", "Leasing model with per-scan billing and CPT code reimbursement", "Portable, lightweight platforms for point-of-care use", "Real-time screening for depression, anxiety, cognitive decline, TBI, PTSD, ADHD"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: New Cumberland, Pennsylvania -> db", "Founded 2003 -> /about", "Founder Michael Zarreii (CEO/CSO) -> /about", "Product ECAT\u2122 point-of-care platform -> /", "Product Intellig-EYES\u2122 neurological platform -> /about", "Manufactured in USA in FDA-registered facility -> /", "FDA-registered certification -> certifications array and /", "U.S. Army funding for four-year study -> /about", "Leasing model with per-scan billing -> /about", "Integration with Epic, Cerner EMR -> /", "Automated tests: Trail Making Test, GPCOG, MMSE, CAPS-5, pupillometry -> /", "Expanding manufacturing capabilities -> /about", "Advisory board includes NCAA CMO, Army colonels, university physicians -> /about", "Patents held and pending -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "ECAT\u2122 is exempt from 510(k) premarket notification and is proudly designed and manufactured in the USA in an FDA-registered facility.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='axon-medical-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='B & H Sheet Metal operates from Asheville, North Carolina, where it has served Western North Carolina since 1976. The company is a second-generation, family-owned and operated fabrication shop that began with rolling, bending, punching, press brake forming, and shearing work.

The shop provides full-service custom sheet metal fabrication, including welding, for both residential and commercial customers. It works with steel, stainless steel, aluminum, copper, and galvanized steel, producing items such as custom chimney caps and stainless steel countertops. All work is custom fabricated; no pre-fabricated products are offered.

Customers include homeowners and contractors throughout Western North Carolina. Typical projects range from residential chimney caps and countertops to commercial fabrication needs. The company emphasizes that no job is too big or too small.

The family ownership stresses pride in material quality and workmanship, offering a warranty on all work and free consultations. They position themselves on competitive pricing and the ability to deliver parts when needed, backed by over 40 years of experience.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rolling", "Bending", "Punching", "Press brake forming", "Shearing", "Welding", "Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Custom metal design"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Copper", "Galvanized steel"], "equipment": ["Press brake", "Shear"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Second-generation family-owned and operated", "All products custom fabricated, no pre-fabricated items", "Warranty on workmanship", "Free consultations available", "Over 40 years of experience serving Western North Carolina"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1976 -> db", "Headquarters Asheville, NC -> db", "Family-owned, second-generation -> /", "Processes: rolling, bending, punching, press brake forming, shearing, welding -> /", "Materials: steel, stainless steel, aluminum, copper, galvanized steel -> /", "Custom fabrication only, no pre-fabricated products -> /", "Serves residential and commercial clients in Western North Carolina -> /", "Examples: custom chimney caps, stainless steel countertops -> /", "Warranty on workmanship -> /", "Free consultations -> /", "Over 40 years experience -> /", "Insured -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "B & H Sheet Metal specializes in metal fabrication and welding services in Asheville, NC.", "founded_year": "1976", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='b-h-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='B & L Scales, Inc. is based in Billings, Montana, and was founded in 1976 by C. Leroy McBride. McBride started the business by traveling across the state on a Goldwing motorcycle with a small trailer of tools, visiting customers and servicing scales and equipment. The company remains family-owned and is now operated by John and Nikki McFerran, with Nikki managing daily operations and John continuing semi-annual service routes across Montana, Wyoming, and parts of Colorado.

The company sells and services a wide range of weighing equipment, from gram-capacity bench scales to truck and rail scales, along with scale indicators. It also supplies meat processing machinery such as grinders, mixers, slicers, smokers, vacuum packers, and associated supplies including cutlery, labels, and seasonings. Technicians hold state licenses in Montana and Wyoming for scale calibration, certification, repair, and placing-in-service reports.

