UPDATE companies SET description='Ball Packaging Products, operating as part of Ball Corporation, is headquartered in Westminster, Colorado. The company maintains a global manufacturing footprint spanning 65-plus plants across 49 countries, with a workforce of approximately 16,000 employees. While the exact founding date of the corporation is not provided in the source material, the business has grown into a major supplier of aluminum packaging.

The company produces aluminum beverage cans, bottles, aerosol cans, ends, and aerosol containers for a range of consumer occasions. Its manufacturing scale is substantial: more than 108 billion units are shipped annually. The product portfolio includes standard and specialty cans for beer, water, and soda, as well as aluminum bottles designed for sporting events and concert venues. A second-generation ReAl® aerosol container technology targeting 75 percent recycled content is slated for launch by 2030.

Primary customers are in the beverage industry, including brands packaging beer, water, and carbonated soft drinks. The company also serves the aerosol market and partners with venues such as stadiums and concert halls. Beyond commercial sales, Ball collaborates with supply-chain partners to advance recycling infrastructure and has set a 2030 goal of achieving a 90 percent global recycling rate for aluminum beverage cans, bottles, and cups, along with an 85 percent average recycled content in its aluminum feedstock.

The Ball Foundation, established in 2011, extends the company’s community impact through grants focused on recycling education, STEM in manufacturing, and disaster relief. The corporation states that its differentiation lies in global scale, sustainability commitments, and innovations such as digital printing on cans and the ReAl® aerosol technology.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Aluminum beverage can manufacturing", "Aluminum bottle manufacturing", "Aerosol can manufacturing", "End manufacturing", "ReAl\u00ae aerosol container technology", "Digital printing on aluminum cans"], "industries": ["Beverage", "Sporting events", "Concert venues", "Aerosol packaging"], "materials": ["Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "108+ billion units annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global network of 65+ manufacturing plants", "Annual shipments exceeding 108 billion units", "2030 sustainability targets: 90% recycling rate, 85% recycled content", "ReAl\u00ae aerosol container with 75% recycled content", "The Ball Foundation supporting recycling education and STEM"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Westminster, Colorado -> db", "16,000 employees worldwide -> page /", "65+ manufacturing plants globally -> page /", "108+ billion units shipped per year -> page /", "49 countries operated in -> page /", "23 languages spoken -> page /", "Products: aluminum beverage cans, bottles, aerosol cans, ends, aerosol containers -> page /", "Sustainability commitments: 90% global recycling rate by 2030, 85% average recycled content by 2030, ReAl\u00ae aerosol container with 75% recycled content by 2030 -> page /", "The Ball Foundation established 2011 -> page /", "Digital printing innovation on cans -> industries_served (db)", "ReAl\u00ae aerosol container technology -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Explore our recyclable products for all use occasions including cans, bottles, ends and aerosol containers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "16,000", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ball-packaging-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bally Ribbon Mills operates from Bally, Pennsylvania, where it has manufactured narrow woven fabrics since 1923. The company began as a specialist in engineered webbing, tapes, and specialty fabrics, and has remained a U.S.-based producer throughout its history.

The firm designs, develops, and weaves a range of products including narrow tapes, webbing, seamless tubular materials, 2-D and 3-D structural shapes, braided structures, and multi-layer composites. Production relies on shuttle looms, needle looms, Jacquard looms, braiding equipment, and specialty broad looms capable of widths up to 72 inches. Post-weave operations cover dyeing, finishing (heat setting, resin treatments, PTFE, silicone, flame retardant), strap cutting, hole punching, sonic welding, and minor sub-assembly. The company states it runs from prototype to full-scale production, though facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

Customers span aerospace, defense, medical, safety, automotive, commercial, and industrial sectors. In aerospace and defense, BRM supplies Mil-Spec webbing and tapes (Mil-W-4088, Mil-DTL-5038K, Mil-W-5625K, Mil-T-87130) that are Berry Amendment compliant. Medical clients receive Class I–III device components such as orthopedic strapping, prosthetic textiles, and dental biotextiles. Safety-market products meet UL and NFPA standards for structural, proximity, and wildland fire-fighting gear.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D','ISO 13485:2016','TS 16949 (compliance)','Berry Amendment compliance','UL standards: CAN/CGSB-155.1-2001, NFPA 1977-2011, NFPA 1971-2013']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Narrow woven tape and webbing production", "Seamless tubular woven materials", "2-Dimensional woven shapes", "3-Dimensional interlocking angles and structures", "Braided structures (flat, biaxial, triaxial, T/J shapes, mandrel over-braids)", "Multi-layer and complex woven shapes", "Uni-directional fabrics", "Shuttle loom weaving", "Needle loom (shuttleless) weaving", "Jacquard loom weaving (CAD-controlled)", "Specialty broadloom weaving (up to 72 inches)", "Yarn dyeing (small lot batch, large lot continuous)", "Finishing: heat setting, scouring, resin treating, PTFE, silicone, latex, waterproof, flame treat, anti-fungal, pre-shrinking", "Strap cutting and sealing", "Hole punching", "Sonic welding", "Minor in-process sub-assemblies", "Prototype development and fabrication", "Product design engineering", "Quality testing: tensile, elongation, color fastness, abrasion", "Berry Amendment compliance documentation", "First article inspection (AS9102)", "FMEA, Control Plans, IQ-OQ-PQ, Lean/Six Sigma"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Medical (Class I, II, III devices)", "Safety (fire fighting protective clothing)", "Automotive", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Composites", "Orthopedic/prosthetic/dental"], "materials": ["Nylon", "Polyester", "Aramid (Kevlar\u00ae, Nomex\u00ae)", "Graphite", "Glass", "Quartz", "Ceramic", "Silicon carbide", "Textured nylon"], "equipment": ["Shuttle looms", "Needle looms (shuttleless looms)", "Jacquard looms (CAD-controlled)", "Braiding machines", "Specialty broad looms (up to 72 inches)", "Spectrophotometers (color matching)", "In-house quality testing laboratory (tensile, elongation, abrasion, color fastness)"], "volume": "Prototype to full-scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Broad weaving capabilities: 2-D/3-D structures, near-net-shape preforms, tapes, webbing from virtually any yarn", "Berry Amendment compliance with 100% traceability for military specifications", "Prototype to full-scale production across aerospace, defense, medical, and safety markets"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1923 in Bally, Pennsylvania -> /about-us", "Manufacturer of engineered woven webbing, tapes, specialty fabrics -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, ISO 13485:2016 -> /quality, /about-us", "Capabilities: shuttle, needle, Jacquard looms; braiding; broadloom up to 72\" -> /capabilities", "Post-weave processes: dyeing, finishing, cutting, hole punching, sonic welding -> /capabilities", "Industries: aerospace, defense, medical, safety, automotive, commercial, industrial, composites -> /about-us, /", "Materials: nylon, polyester, aramid (Kevlar, Nomex), graphite, glass, quartz, ceramic, silicon carbide -> /about-us, /", "Mil-Spec products: Mil-W-4088, Mil-DTL-5038K, Mil-W-5625K, Mil-T-87130 -> /", "Medical: Class I-III device components, orthopedic, prosthetic, dental biotextiles -> /, /about-us", "Safety: UL/NFPA standards for fire fighting gear -> /quality", "Volume: prototype to full-scale production -> /, /about-us", "Quality: 24/7 in-house lab, AS9102 first articles, FMEA, Lean/Six Sigma -> /quality", "Berry Amendment compliance with traceability -> /quality, /", "3-D weaving pioneers, 70+ years experience -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1923, Bally Ribbon Mills (BRM) has been involved in the design, development, and manufacture of highly specialized engineered woven webbing, tapes, and specialty fabrics.", "founded_year": "1923", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/bally-ribbon-mills/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bally-ribbon-mills' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Baltimore Aircoil Company (BAC) is headquartered in Milford, Delaware, and traces its origins to 1938 when a single cooling coil was hand-built in a founder’s garage. The company has since evolved into an employee-owned enterprise, with its workforce of more than 2,000 global team members holding ownership stakes.

BAC designs and manufactures sustainable comfort cooling, process cooling, and refrigeration equipment for demanding environments. Its product portfolio includes evaporative condensers, adiabatic coolers such as the Trillium™ TRFS for large-scale data centers, modular hybrid coolers like the Nexus® line with integrated PuriStream™ water treatment, and a range of replacement parts supported by inspection services.

The company serves a variety of industries, with explicit focus on heavy industrial and energy sectors. Recent project announcements highlight deployments in large-scale data centers, while its refrigeration piping manuals target industrial refrigeration system designers.

BAC’s stated mission is to “continually advance truly sustainable cooling – inspired by nature, powered by our people.” The firm emphasizes balancing water and energy savings, a commitment dating to its first coil, and frames its differentiation around a coordinated, non-transactional process aimed at getting the solution right the first time and maintaining performance for decades. Core values include courage, innovation, responsibility, and trust.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Comfort cooling system design and manufacturing", "Process cooling system design and manufacturing", "Refrigeration system design and manufacturing", "Evaporative cooling equipment manufacturing", "Adiabatic cooling equipment manufacturing", "Hybrid cooling equipment manufacturing", "Water treatment system integration", "Parts supply and inspection", "Equipment lifecycle support and maintenance guidance"], "industries": ["Heavy Industrial", "Energy", "Data Centers"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Trillium\u2122 Adiabatic Cooler TRFS", "Nexus\u00ae Modular Hybrid Cooler", "PuriStream\u2122 Water Treatment System", "Evaporative Condenser"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1938 -> db, /about", "Headquartered in Milford, Delaware -> db", "Employee-owned -> /about", "More than 2,000 global team members -> /about", "Products: Trillium\u2122 Adiabatic Cooler TRFS, Nexus\u00ae Modular Hybrid Cooler, PuriStream\u2122 Water Treatment System -> / (news)", "Serves Heavy Industrial & Energy industries -> db (industries_served)", "Provides comfort cooling, process cooling, refrigeration solutions -> db (description), /about", "Global presence with region selector -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We create sustainable comfort cooling, process cooling, and refrigeration solutions for the most essential and demanding environments on earth.", "founded_year": "1938", "employee_count": "more than 2,000", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/baltimore-aircoil-company/"], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='baltimore-aircoil-company-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
